# Cline Rules - Project Conventions

## Comment Block Headers
When creating comment section headers in code files, ALWAYS use this format:

```
// =========================================================
// SECTION TITLE HERE
// =========================================================
```

NEVER use this broken format (missing closing `//`):
```
// =========================================================
// SECTION TITLE HERE
========================================================= */
```

The closing separator line must also have `//` prefix and should NOT have `*/` suffix unless it's actually a block comment being closed.

## Documentation
When finished a task, always update markdown files like README.md